    description: "**Mechanism.** Spec lines 234 & 278 document AnalysisRun.version as e.g. 'hypergumbo-0.1.0' (WITH the hypergumbo- prefix), but the 83 conforming ARs emit bare '5.0.1' (NO prefix). Meanwhile limits.analyzer_version = 'hypergumbo-5.0.1' (prefixed) and reproducibility_context.captured.hypergumbo_version = '5.0.1' (bare). So three in-map surfaces carrying the tool version disagree on whether it is prefixed: AR.version bare / limits.analyzer_version prefixed / captured.hypergumbo_version bare, and none matches the spec's prefixed example.\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer joining AR.version against limits.analyzer_version for an equality check ('did this AR run under the declared analyzer version') fails on the hypergumbo- prefix mismatch.\n\n**Related (distinct).** Family of the WI-luhur version-field drifts but the AR.version prefix-vs-spec / cross-surface prefix disagreement is named in no ledger row (WI-mipul=pass_version, WI-mifok=pass_version absence, the play-routes-version='1' row=the singleton outlier value). Cross-link to the card-007 play-routes row. Source: dogfood_tranche_07 F124.A2, deterministic frozen read."  # e9bc
